<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Rules forced Fairfax sale - Hollinger.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Rules forced Fairfax sale - Hollinger.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian media group Hollinger International Inc said on Monday, the sale of its 25 percent stake in John Fairfax Holdings Ltd was prompted by suggestions the Australian government would not review foreign ownership limitations in the media sector.</p>
<p>Earlier, New Zealand investment group, Brierley Investments Ltd said it would pay an average of A$2.82 per share for 20 percent of Fairfax from Hollinger International, and would approach Fairfax shareholders for approval to buy Hollinger's remaining five percent stake.</p>
</text>
